        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-07T16:34:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am a little hesitant about defining the struct like this since someone could accidentally create one of the stack or create multiple and this have a large payload for response_buffer.\n\nI think just creating a static response_buffer the size of IPC_MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE is a litte more safe, and then we can cast it to what ever structure we need.\n\n\nMaybe we define this as\n\ncros_ec_ishtp_msg {\n  struct cros_ec_ishtp_msg_hdr hdr;\n  uint8_t data[0];\n} __ec_align4;\n\n\nand still have\n\nstatic uint8_t response_buffer[IPC_MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE] __aligned(4);\n\nthen we can cast like:\n\nstruct cros_ec_ishtp_msg *out \u003d (void*) response_buffer;\nout-\u003ehrd.command \u003d 1;",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 42,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "ff8210ca226b2e0d9beeb2938e1e3319ee67b62a",
